            {
              "id": "43a7386e-39b3-349a-9620-a78521c71906",
              "name": "Xml Parsing Library May Allow Xxe Attacks",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "\"XML Parsing Library Vulnerability: Disable External Entity Resolution to Avoid XXE Attacks\"\n\n## Standalone Example (not your code)\n\n_A self-contained program written to illustrate this weakness, not taken from your project. Depending on the finding it may reproduce the vulnerable pattern, show the fix, or both; apply the Recommended Code Fix above to your code._\n\n## Description\n\nXML External Entity (XXE) attacks occur when an application processing XML input allows the inclusion of dynamic content that is referenced by an external entity. These entities can be used to disclose internal files, internal port scanning, remote code execution, and denial of service attacks. In JavaScript, when using libraries like `libxmljs` to parse XML data, if the parsing process is not properly configured, it can lead to XXE attacks.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate XXE attacks, it's recommended to disable the resolution of external entities in the XML parser configuration. If the application needs to parse XML input, consider the following:\n\n- Use less complex data formats such as JSON, and avoid serialization of sensitive data.\n- Patch or upgrade all XML processors and libraries in use by the application or on the underlying operating system. Use dependency checkers.\n- Use XML Schema Definition to validate input.\n- Verify XML or XSL file upload functionality against XEE and/or XXE.\n- SAST tools can help detect XXE in source code, although it's possible to have false positives and negatives.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix this vulnerability in the provided code, you should disable the resolution of external entities in the XML parser configuration. Here is an example of how to do this with `libxmljs`:\n\n```javascript\nvar libxmljs = require(\"libxmljs\");\nvar xml = \"<root></root>\";\nvar xmlDoc = libxmljs.parseXml(xml, { noblanks: true, noent: true, nocdata: true });\n```\n\nIn this example, the `noent` option is set to `true` to disable the resolution of external entities.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe only library dependency required by the code example to execute properly is `libxmljs`.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XXE Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference ('XXE')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-611",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-611"
                ]
              }
