            {
              "id": "cf351ee9-72c0-3a39-a678-efd0b8996fd3",
              "name": "Database Query Without Field Selection Exposes Data",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "Unselected Field Database Query Vulnerability\n\n## Standalone Example (not your code)\n\n_A self-contained program written to illustrate this weakness, not taken from your project. Depending on the finding it may reproduce the vulnerable pattern, show the fix, or both; apply the Recommended Code Fix above to your code._\n\n## Description\n\n\"Unselected Field Database Query Vulnerability\" in JavaScript is a security flaw that occurs when a developer does not specify the fields to be returned from a database query. This can lead to the exposure of sensitive data. For instance, if a user object in the database contains a password field, and a query is made to fetch all users without specifying the fields to be returned, the password field will be included in the response.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, developers should always specify the fields to be returned in a database query. This can be done by passing an object to the `attributes` option in the query, where the keys are the field names and the values are true if the field should be returned and false otherwise.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is how you can fix the vulnerability in the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ndb.User.findAll({\n  attributes: ['id', 'username', 'email'] // specify the fields to be returned\n}).then(users => {\n  // ...\n});\n```\n\nIn this example, only the 'id', 'username', and 'email' fields will be returned in the query.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Sequelize: A promise-based Node.js ORM for Postgres, MySQL, MariaDB, SQLite, and Microsoft SQL Server.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-209: Information Exposure Through an Error Message](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/209.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
