            {
              "id": "e4109124-a7e3-3004-8776-aa4f6b683e25",
              "name": "Weak Cryptographic Hash Algorithm Used",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "Insecure Cryptographic Hash Identified: MD5, SHA1 Inadequate for Security; bcrypt, scrypt, Argon2 Recommended for Passwords, SHA-256+ for Integrity Checks.\n\n## Standalone Example (not your code)\n\n_A self-contained program written to illustrate this weakness, not taken from your project. Depending on the finding it may reproduce the vulnerable pattern, show the fix, or both; apply the Recommended Code Fix above to your code._\n\n## Description\n\nInsecure Cryptographic Hash Identified: MD5, SHA1 Inadequate for Security; bcrypt, scrypt, Argon2 Recommended for Passwords, SHA-256+ for Integrity Checks is a vulnerability that arises when cryptographic hash functions with known weaknesses, such as MD5 and SHA1, are used in security-critical contexts. These hash functions are considered insecure due to their susceptibility to collision attacks, where two different inputs produce the same hash output. This can lead to unauthorized access or data integrity issues.\n\nIn JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when using libraries such as 'md5' to hash sensitive data like passwords. \n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use stronger cryptographic hash functions. For password hashing, bcrypt, scrypt, or Argon2 are recommended due to their resistance to brute-force and rainbow table attacks. For integrity checks, SHA-256 or higher is recommended.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the 'md5' library with a more secure hashing library. Here is an example using 'bcrypt':\n\n```javascript\nvar bcrypt = require('bcrypt');\nvar saltRounds = 10;\n\nbcrypt.hash('myPassword', saltRounds, function(err, hash) {\n  // Store hash in your password DB.\n});\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe 'bcrypt' library is required for the code example to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Password Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## CWE\n\nThis vulnerability is related to [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)."
