            {
              "id": "ed4592b8-8077-3651-939b-39c3fa4ff342",
              "name": "Insecure Default Session Cookie Name",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nSession cookie name fingerprinting occurs when an application uses the framework's default session cookie name. The default name can reveal implementation details to an attacker and help them select targeted attacks.\n\nConfigure an application-specific, non-descriptive session cookie name instead of accepting the default. The shown session configuration should also use a secret supplied through protected configuration, avoid creating sessions for anonymous requests, and protect the cookie with HTTPS-only, HttpOnly, and SameSite settings.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nSet the session middleware name option to a unique, application-specific value that does not identify the framework. Generate SESSION_SECRET with a cryptographically secure random generator, store it in a secret manager or protected environment variable, and rotate it according to the application's secret-management process. Enable secure cookies in production and configure Express trust proxy only when the application is deployed behind a trusted TLS-terminating proxy. Use a production-ready shared session store rather than the default in-memory store.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~javascript\nconst session = require('express-session');\n\nif (!process.env.SESSION_SECRET || process.env.SESSION_SECRET.length < 32) {\n  throw new Error('SESSION_SECRET must be set to a strong random value');\n}\n\napp.set('trust proxy', 1);\napp.use(session({\n  name: 'app_sid',\n  secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET,\n  resave: false,\n  saveUninitialized: false,\n  cookie: {\n    secure: true,\n    httpOnly: true,\n    sameSite: 'lax',\n    maxAge: 60 * 60 * 1000\n  }\n}));\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~javascript\nnpm install express-session\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Session Management Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n- [express-session documentation](https://expressjs.com/en/resources/middleware/session.html)\n\n## Standalone Example (not your code)\n\n_A self-contained program written to illustrate this weakness, not taken from your project. Depending on the finding it may reproduce the vulnerable pattern, show the fix, or both; apply the Recommended Code Fix above to your code._\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"express-session-cookie-name-demo\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node app.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"express\": \"^4.21.2\",\n    \"express-session\": \"^1.18.1\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```javascript\n// app.js\nconst express = require('express');\nconst session = require('express-session');\n\nconst app = express();\nconst port = 3000;\n\n// Intentionally vulnerable demonstration:\n// No `name` option is supplied, so express-session uses its default\n// cookie name: \"connect.sid\".\napp.use(session({\n  secret: 'keyboard cat',\n  resave: true,\n  saveUninitialized: true,\n  cookie: { secure: false }\n}));\n\napp.get('/', (req, res) => {\n  req.session.views = (req.session.views || 0) + 1;\n\n  res.json({\n    message: 'Session created',\n    views: req.session.views,\n    note: 'Inspect the Set-Cookie response header for the default connect.sid cookie name.'\n  });\n});\n\napp.listen(port, () => {\n  console.log(`Vulnerable demo listening at http://localhost:${port}`);\n  console.log(`Test with: curl -i http://localhost:${port}/`);\n});\n```\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm start\ncurl -i http://localhost:3000/\n```\n\nThe response includes a header similar to:\n\n```http\nSet-Cookie: connect.sid=s%3A...; Path=/; HttpOnly\n```\n\nThe `connect.sid` name fingerprints the application as using `express-session`."
              },
