              "id": "fca7bab8-6ef9-3e6b-8613-c6bdf1ebf8c2",
              "name": "Promise Without Catch Handler",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability\n\n## Standalone Example (not your code)\n\n_A self-contained program written to illustrate this weakness, not taken from your project. Depending on the finding it may reproduce the vulnerable pattern, show the fix, or both; apply the Recommended Code Fix above to your code._\n\n## Description\n\nUnhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability in JavaScript occurs when a promise is rejected but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the error. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, crashes, and potential security vulnerabilities. In the provided code, the promise returned by `db.Product.findAll()` is not being handled for potential rejections.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always handle promise rejections by providing a `.catch()` block or by using `try/catch` with async/await. This allows you to handle errors gracefully and prevent unexpected application behavior.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a fixed version of the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ndb.Product.findAll()\n  .then(products => {\n    output = {\n      products: products\n    }\n    res.render('app/products', {\n      output: output\n    })\n  })\n  .catch(err => {\n    // Handle the error here\n    console.error(err);\n    res.status(500).send('An error occurred');\n  });\n```\n\nIn this version, a `.catch()` block is added to handle any errors that may occur when fetching products from the database.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to be using Sequelize (for `db.Product.findAll()`) and Express (for `res.render()`). Therefore, the following libraries are required:\n\n- Sequelize\n- Express\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
              },
